cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its pre-registered design, please cite it as below. Results are pending until the study has been run; cite the pre-registration tag, not this file, for any claim about outcomes."
title: "Reward hacking under GRPO: discoverability, reward and monitor effects (pre-registered small-scale replication-extension)"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Luca Engel"
keywords:
  - reward hacking
  - GRPO
  - pre-registration
  - LoRA
  - Qwen3
abstract: "A small-scale (Qwen3-1.7B, LoRA-GRPO, at most 5 seeds per arm), pre-registered replication-extension of the run_tests()-overwrite reward-hacking setting of Wong et al.: it separates prompt-wording effects from reward effects, measures a discoverability dose-response with the seed as the unit, and tests displacement under a deliberately leaky syntactic monitor."
